{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794050396,"nonce":"hl8BtUaYCiafjKMkF7ZExmsoHwU=","title":"A sign-off gate whose only dependent is when-excluded is skipped before its needs run","message":"2c37802 skips a waiting gate whose dependents are all terminal. A gate whose only dependent is excluded by `when:` counts as such a gate. It is skipped as \"no longer needed\" on the first tick, before its own `needs` (for example `build`) have run. The Run then settles Succeeded and nobody was asked.\n\nNo authority is handed out. But an author who meant the gate as a sign-off on the build gets no sign-off.\n\nQuestion: should the skip wait for the gate's own needs to finish, or apply only when a dependent failed?\n\nEvidence: red team (CC-4/B1 refuted), scratch test .workspaces/afk-redteam/crates/scarab-server/tests/redteam_unneeded_gate.rs:26.","files":null}]}